PLAIN-ENGLISH SUMMARY (NOT LEGALLY BINDING — see clauses 1-11 below)
==================================================================

This summary exists so a procurement or legal reviewer can decide in
30 seconds whether they need to read further. The binding terms are
in clauses 1-11. Where this summary and those clauses conflict, the
clauses control.

  * MEMSCOPE IS FREE FOR ANY USE, INCLUDING COMMERCIAL USE INSIDE A
    COMPANY. The `memscope-fw` distribution published on the Python
    Package Index (PyPI) is free of charge. No payment, no licence
    key, no seat count, no time limit, no per-user fee, no feature
    locked behind a purchase. Individuals, contractors, startups,
    and large enterprises may install it and run every command it
    ships with, for any internal business purpose, indefinitely.

  * YOU DO NOT NEED TO CONTACT US TO USE IT. There is nothing to
    purchase, register, activate, or renew, and no licence key to
    obtain. Install it and use it. (On first run the Software shows
    a short summary of these terms and asks you to accept it once;
    that is the only step, it happens locally, and nothing is
    transmitted.)

  * IT RUNS ENTIRELY ON YOUR MACHINE. The Software makes no network
    calls in normal operation. Your build artifacts, symbol names,
    file paths, and reports never leave your computer.

  * SOURCE CODE IS NOT DISTRIBUTED. MemScope is not open source and
    is not licensed under any OSI-approved or FSF-recognised licence.
    You receive the binary distribution and the right to use it under
    clauses 1-11.

  * WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO: redistribute or resell it, or strip the
    copyright and licence notices. See clause 4 for the full list.
    Using it inside your company, on as many machines as you like,
    is expressly permitted.

  * NEED SOMETHING WE DON'T SHIP? Custom extensions and bespoke
    engineering work are available by arrangement, are NOT part of
    this Agreement, and are licensed separately as their own
    software. Just email dumitrescu.adrian121@gmail.com and we will
    discuss what you need. Nothing about that conversation changes
    your right to keep using the free Software under this Agreement.

End of summary. The binding agreement begins below.


